    "paragraph": "An agent-based simulation model was developed to project changes in trajectory diversity from 2026 to 2036 across China, Russia, Japan, the United Kingdom, and the United States. Another study evaluated three transportation interventions in Boston and New York City using both traditional geographic distance and mobility-network exposure to show how human mobility shapes the spread of urban policy effects. Finally, researchers developed Wellbeing-Former, a reasoning model designed to measure flood-related wellbeing across Ireland using public discourse.",
